Make sure CalibrationContext gets copied to actor.

In the overload of KalmanFitter::fit taking a vector of Surface*,
make sure that CalibrationContext (and freeToBoundCorrection) gets
copied from the options to the actor.  This was done in the previous
overload but was apparently forgotten here.

If we don't do this, we'll end up initializing a reference to the
CalibrationContxt, dereferencing the null pointer.

While we were apparently never actually doing anything with this null
reference (and thus not crashing), this does provoke a warning
from the undefined behavior sanitizer in debug builds, which causes
test failures in FPGATrackSimConfTools:

```
/afs/cern.ch/work/s/ssnyder/acts/acts/Core/include/Acts/TrackFitting/KalmanFitter.hpp:616:14: runtime error: reference binding to null pointer of type 'const struct CalibrationContext'
...
```

However, this has generally been hidden by the fact that in the CI in dbg
builds, the tests tend to time out before they get to this point (and there
are also other assertion failures ahead of it...).
